   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Poder», «querer» and «saber»",
     "texto": [
      "**Poder** (to be able): **pude**, **pudeste**, **pôde**. **Querer** (to want): **quis**, **quiseste**, **quisemos**. **Saber** (to know): **soube**, **soubeste**.",
      "In the past, **saber** means «to find out»: **soube** = I found out. And with **não** in the past, **não quis** = he / she didn't want to."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Trazer» and «ler»",
     "texto": [
      "**Trazer** (to bring): **trouxe** (I brought), **trouxeste** (you brought). **Ler** (to read): **li** (I read), **leste** (you read), **leu** (he / she read).",
      "Watch out: in Portugal **li** is pronounced «lee»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
